# Reviewing changes in `prompts/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`prompts/REVIEW.md`** for any
changed path under `prompts/`. That map cites rule IDs from `prompts/AGENTS.md` (e.g.
`H1`, `AP-3`) — it never restates the rule text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D2 AP-3 (`detect_anti_patterns`) — never hardcode a prompt string in Python; all
  prompts are `.j2` files rendered via `PromptService.render_prompt()` (H1).
- D2 naming/config-split — `{component}_system_prompt.j2` naming; no numeric thresholds
  in templates (LLM-judged).

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
